W44-182 CfL AC tile aggregation probe — ROOT CAUSE IDENTIFIED
==================================================================
Date: 2026-05-21
Image: clic_097cb426 (1024×1024)
Effort: 7 Distance: 5
Tile grid: 16×16 (each = 8×8 blocks = 64×64 px)
Encoder: EncoderStrategy::Zenjxl

Headline
--------
**The clic_097cb426 right-column SSIM2 -7 deficit is caused by our CfL
Newton solver producing ALL ZEROS for ytox across the entire image,
while cjxl produces nonzero ytox at 134-186 of 256 tiles.**

Specifically: our `find_best_multiplier_newton_*` (`jxl-encoder-simd/src/cfl.rs`)
uses parameters `NEWTON_EPS_DEFAULT = 1.0`, `NEWTON_MAX_ITERS_DEFAULT = 10`,
warm-starts from `ls_x`, and **falls back to `ls_x` on non-convergence**.
libjxl `enc_chroma_from_luma.cc:152-171` uses `eps = 100`, `max_iters = 20`,
starts from `x = 0`, and **uses whatever `x` is at the last iteration**
(no fallback). The "eps=100 causes oscillation" docstring claim is
falsified by direct measurement on clic_097cb426 e7 d=5.

Per-channel divergence vs cjxl:
- Pass 1 (compute_cfl_map, forced DCT8 + Newton at e>=7):
  - ytox: ours 0/256 nonzero vs cjxl 186/256 nonzero
  - ytob: ours 90/256 nonzero (mean -2.73) vs cjxl 86/256 nonzero (mean -0.06)
- Pass 2 (refine_cfl_map, real ac_strategy + raw_quant_field):
  - ytox: ours 0/256 nonzero vs cjxl 134/256 nonzero
  - ytob: ours 78/256 nonzero (mean -4.98) vs cjxl 167/256 nonzero (mean -2.93)

Per-pass divergent-tile counts (ours vs cjxl):
- Pass 1: ytox 186/256 divergent (72.7%), ytob 164/256 (64.1%)
- Pass 2: ytox 134/256 divergent (52.3%), ytob 108/256 (42.2%)

Per-pass mean |Δ|:
- Pass 1: mean |Δytox| = 2.84, mean |Δytob| = 4.31
- Pass 2: mean |Δytox| = 2.75, mean |Δytob| = 2.39

The Pass-1 → Pass-2 narrowing happens because cjxl's pass 2 re-converges
some ytox tiles back to 0 (cjxl pass-1 has 186 nonzero, pass-2 has 134),
while ours stays at 0 in both passes.

